WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.145
The Design phase turns analysis into a learning plan.

00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:06.760
This is where course creators define learning objectives, performance outcomes,

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.515
module sequence, instructional strategy, examples, practice opportunities,

00:00:10.515 --> 00:00:14.860
assessment approach, narration plan, visual direction, and accessibility expectations.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.550
The design should explain how the course will help learners move from current performance

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.720
to desired performance.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.550
Learning objectives should be specific enough to guide development.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.540
A vague objective such as understand the policy is hard to teach and hard to assess.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.920
A stronger objective describes what learners will be able to identify, choose, apply,

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.670
compare, perform, or explain.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.825
The objective becomes a filter for content: if a detail does not support the objective,

00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:39.895
it may belong in a reference document instead of the main course.

00:00:39.895 --> 00:00:40.955
Course structure matters.

00:00:40.955 --> 00:00:45.630
Modules should build in a logical order, usually from context to concepts to application.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.925
Examples make abstract content concrete.

00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:51.400
Practice gives learners a chance to use the information before the final assessment.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.675
Assessments should measure the same knowledge or decisions the course teaches.

00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:58.655
Alignment is the core design discipline: objectives, content, practice, media,

00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:01.040
and assessment should point in the same direction.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.466
Storyboards make the design visible before production becomes expensive.

00:01:04.466 --> 00:01:09.080
A storyboard can show screen flow, narration, visual ideas, interactions, feedback,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.000
and quiz alignment.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.180
It gives stakeholders something to review before the team records audio,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.786
builds complex interactions, or creates final media.

00:01:15.786 --> 00:01:17.368
A storyboard is not busywork;

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:20.240
it is a way to catch problems while they are still cheap to fix.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.840
Accessibility should be planned here, not added at the end.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.400
Decisions about captions, transcripts, keyboard navigation, alt text, reading order,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.960
contrast, plain language, and media alternatives all affect design.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.880
A strong design phase makes the learner experience clearer before development begins.
